{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1465259-ratkin-and-breeding-through-the-ages","id":1465259,"title":"Ratkin and breeding through the ages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-25T03:11:43-07:00","id":1465259,"title":"Ratkin and breeding through the ages","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I'd like to ask for your oppinion about the breeding of Ratkin with rats, more correctly rattus genus.<br /> <br /> There are two distict types of rats currently in Europe &amp; America, who live together with humans &amp; a viable Kinfolk of the Ratkin:<br /> 1) Rattus rattus, the &quot;black&quot;; &quot;ship&quot;;... rat. This species were responsible for the Black Death and came earlier to Europe than the...<br /> &quot;) Rattus norvegicus, the &quot;brown&quot;; &quot;wharf&quot;; &quot;sever&quot; rat. They are better adapted to the environment than the 1) and could take over much of the habitat of them. Intrestingly they are not a vector of bubonic plague, what prevented bigger epidemics.<br /> <br /> The two species can't breed, BUT Ratkins had Kinfolk in both parties.<br /> Does that mean, that the wererats can cross the boundary of species and have litters with both? (Red Talons did such feats with dingos and cape hunting dogs.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T07:23:33-07:00","id":1465274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1465259-ratkin-and-breeding-through-the-ages#post1465259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The two species can't breed, BUT Ratkins had Kinfolk in both parties.<br /> Does that mean, that the wererats can cross the boundary of species and have litters with both? (Red Talons did such feats with dingos and cape hunting dogs.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on your own example, i'd be tempted to say yes, indeed. What i'd guess could lead to a degree of genetic drifting between kinfolk populations of the two species ocurring through reproduction with wandering Ratkin.<br /> <br /> Maybe even the formation of subspecies with hybrid qualities in some locales with a large roving population of ratkin.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though debating Fera breeds x speciation can be a confusing subject, based on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_wild_dog#Evolution\" target=\"_blank\">some evidence</a>. Coyotes are closer to wolves &amp; dogs than golden jackals or african wild dogs (from which cape hunting dogs are a subspecies), though dingos might be closer than either though information is scant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-25-2021, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T07:37:28-07:00","id":1465276,"title":"","content":"Garou do the same with wolf species already. Indeed they went further already, as they did in Africa and, more extremely, in Australia, where the Thylacine, similarities aside is actually more distant from a wolf than apes are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T08:48:23-07:00","id":1465284,"title":"","content":"Dingos are really just wolves in another part of the world, and they're endangered because they can so easily breed with dogs and dilute their genes. <br /> <br /> <br /> Rokea, Mokole and Nagah are greater examples of &quot;lots of breeds that can't interbreed&quot; <br /> Ratkin, like the Foxes, are really questionable as it's a case of &quot;why this breed but not all these other breeds&quot; because there are a lot of Rat kinds out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T09:31:25-07:00","id":1465286,"title":"","content":"Thylacines aren't dingos, and they're already extinct, they were the preferred Bunyip stock. They are marsupials, though, similar to wolves just by convergent evolution, but genetically diverged since the earliest days of the mammals. Wolves are more genetically similar to humans than to Thylacines. Among all the mammalian Fera this is the biggest species gap.<br /> <br /> I would have to research the matter, but I suspect the gap on the Mokol\u00e9 is even greater, it is just that we don't pay as much attention to reptiles. Not to say that they theoretically came from dinosaurs, which should put them nearer birds than modern reptiles, but no one knew that back then.<br /> <br /> On the Ananasi, Corax and Rokea I have no idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T10:41:53-07:00","id":1465296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1465259-ratkin-and-breeding-through-the-ages?p=1465276#post1465276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou do the same with wolf species already. Indeed they went further already, as they did in Africa and, more extremely, in Australia, where the Thylacine, similarities aside is actually more distant from a wolf than apes are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never seriously looked into the Bunyip = Thylacine part of the lore. Truth be told, because as you pointed out it's ludricous like heck and then some.<br /> <br /> If i ever made an Australia game would either associate the Bunyip with dingoes - and keep the &quot;possibly destroyed by kinfolk dispute with the Talons&quot; angle - or treat them as a whole different kind of Fera instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:18:38-07:00","id":1465303,"title":"","content":"Lots of things don't make sense when it comes to the animal breeds. It's really a part of the game where it's just best for STs to do whatever makes the most sense for them.<br /> <br /> I made an early decision in the chronicles I run to just make the Bunyip their own Thylacine-based Fera breed. They are considered to be &quot;honorary&quot; Garou because the tribes that wiped them out in Australia felt guilty about it and passed the decision at a Concolation in Jindabyne in the hopes to assuage their spirits in chiminage (it failed, the Bunyip spirits are still angry). Slowly that resolution was passed along subsequent Concolations elsewhere so that it's been recognized by most of the Garou Nation at this point. To make it official, there'd need to be an Imperial Moot but those haven't been held since 1855.<br /> <br /> I also never liked the idea of Garou including dingos and painted dogs and other nonsense so I simply don't allow it. Mamu and his Red Talon pack do look like dingoes, but that's because of a fetish they have, not from interbreeding with them. In fact, many Australian Garou use the same fetish to protect the Veil.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed Silent Striders are jackals though, but the less Pure Breed they have the more they look like wolves because of interbreeding. The Garou are more like a &quot;were-canid&quot; group, but there still needs to be significant ability to interbreed with each other in the wild.<br /> <br /> I always thought Ratkin was too much of a fantasy concept than a gothic horror one supposedly based on real world legends. So I eliminated them from my chronicles. But I do have fomori based on wererats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T13:28:52-07:00","id":1465316,"title":"","content":"Thylacine shenanigans aside, most Fera have this trend of including species that shouldn't be able to interbreed, but the writers rarely tried to make biological sense.<br /> <br /> Ghural cover several species of bears, Kitsune several species of foxes. Keep in mind that foxes are Canidae, so if Garou can mate with wolf and jackal alike, why can't they with foxes? Just 'cause.<br /> <br /> Mokol\u00e9 cover so many species, and in the Ananasi they barely considered species at all.<br /> <br /> On the Bastet, on the other side, they went full mode &quot;every species is an almost entirely new Fera&quot;. Again, just 'cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T22:34:37-07:00","id":1465359,"title":"","content":"Mokol\u00e9 and Bunyip are tricky.<br /> <br /> Mokol\u00e9 has a rare Gift (in the Breedbook, called Steal Shape(?), what allows them to change their breed form, so they could follow the evolution and did not go extcint.<br /> <br /> Bunyip received help from the Mokol\u00e9 (see Shattered Dreams &amp; Apocalyptic Record) and - with a Rite - changed their spirit/flesh to became a were-dog-headed pouched dogs.<br /> <br /> Gurahl are also intresting. The Okuma had even giant panda among their Kin. Rokea also embrace almost all sharks.<br /> <br /> Coyotes and wolves can interbreed &amp; have fertile offspring. Genomic studies show that all grey wolves in North America has some coyote in them. So much for the Pure Breed... (And a high five for the Nuwisha!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 10-26-2021, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T23:23:40-07:00","id":1465360,"title":"","content":"Ananasi didn't get the species considerations because of the weirdness of Crawlerling and how they incorporate new bodies into it, as the werespiders are like arachnid Borg in that regard.<br /> <br /> Switch topic!<br /> <br /> Things about Garou that studies suggest should happen - <br /> <br /> Every sept has a literal Nuwisha cousin or two. Everyone knows, at a certain rank, but doesn't talk about it.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords nervously try to assure everyone with posturing that they are not, in fact, part dog.<br /> <br /> As the Red Talons eschewed breeding with humanity before agriculture was ever in sight, none among them has pale skin or passes for white in homid. Some new cubs in colonial holdings believe that human authorities can sense that they're werewolves even in Homid, until a Bone Gnawer, CoG or other knowledgeable authority sits them down for a talk about how humans see skin color...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T00:27:20-07:00","id":1465362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1465259-ratkin-and-breeding-through-the-ages?p=1465360#post1465360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ananasi didn't get the species considerations because of the weirdness of Crawlerling and how they incorporate new bodies into it, as the werespiders are like arachnid Borg in that regard...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ananasi have a Merit which let them to change their original spider species and can breed with any spider. For them it's easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T05:06:02-07:00","id":1465383,"title":"","content":"It's also good to remember that most Fera are actually older than the entire humanity, according to lore and following the actual origin of their other species. So it's not only about their animal counterpart.<br /> <br /> What they shapeshifted into before us?<br /> <br /> That's a tricky question. Grey wolves alone are 1 million years old as a species, while we're 150-300 thousands. But depending on how you read lore, Garou may come from earlier wolves, and those go back about 60 million years in the past. 1 million years ago they would have early Homini genus to shift into, but more than 6 million they wouldn't have even Australopithecus.<br /> <br /> And yeah, curiously wolves breed true with dogs and coyotes. But they don't with jackals, AFAIK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T08:38:09-07:00","id":1465407,"title":"","content":"Things I can't stress enough<br /> <br /> Dingoes are genetically super-compatible with wolves and dogs. They're the same thing but like... blond. If the Garou were to ever have a second type of canine alongside the grey wolf, it'd be Dingoes. <br /> <br /> Foxes are pretty far off wolves and dogs. <br /> Kitsune only exist for one fox breed, the red fox (silver/black foxes are just Red foxes with different pigments) You don't see kitsune artic foxes or desert foxes. Kitsune only happen in Asia because... Americans fetishize Asia too much. <br /> <br /> Thyclaine might as well be aliens. Their only common point is that they're mammals, but they're marsupials and that's a divergence long, long, long ago. It would be completely accurate to say Cats are closer to wolves than Thyclaines. <br /> <br /> <br /> How WTA decided on breeds is, well, stupid, and entirely based on mortal perceptions rather than genetics. But the changing breeds are all half-human so maybe that's something worth considering. If two rokea of radically different types of sharks want to get it on, they can do it comfortably in Homid, and their baby can be the mother's breed. There's also a sense of location since we're talking about magical spirits rather than genetics most of the time; With homids of breeds like the Anasai, they're probably going to be mystically influenced by their surroundings to become a local variant of spider; The local spider spirits might say so. I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T10:34:45-07:00","id":1465420,"title":"","content":"One of the things Forsaken did better was to write off biological wolves from the get go, so they can work on proper werewolf themes without worrying about biology. The Uratha are not, in any regard, part wolf.<br /> <br /> But Apocalypse have this aspect. Too much of the game already delves into biology and animal behavior, even (or especially) when the authors get it all wrong. The problem now would be how to address the issue without defacing the game. Just ignoring the issue was the main answer up to now (not the only one, as we got the Rite for the Bunyip mating with Thylacines).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}